BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Financial Planning for Business: Entrepreneurship 
 for New Canadians
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T193000
UID:6a8db7cf36204e08fbb70d05@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month.\nJoin us online with the
 \nCanadian Foundation for Financial Planning.\nThis workshop introduces th
 e essentials of launching a business\, including Goods and Services Tax 
 (GST)\, Harmonized Sales Tax (HST)\, Employment Insurance (EI)\, raising
  capital\, and choosing the right business structure.\nRegistration:\nTh
 is virtual Zoom event is free to join. Once registered\, you’ll receive 
 an email with the Zoom link.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and partici
 pating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8db7cf36204e08fbb70d05
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
