BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DJ At Any Age: Memories in the Mix
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6aa062565ecd9e1b553241c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring out your inner DJ in this intergenerational program for 
 seniors and adults. Learn basic djing skills and connect with others over 
 a shared love of music. Artist and educator Deejay Vee from At Any Age wil
 l teach you how to use a dj controller and software in a fun and relaxed a
 tmosphere. Working individually or in pairs\, you'll create and exchange p
 laylists of songs that represent meaningful moments in your life.\nNo prio
 r experience needed.\nThis 5-week program series takes place every Thursda
 y from November 12th – December 10th.\nWeeks 1 – 4: Learn DJing skills
 .\nWeek 5: Showcase! Perform your new skills for the group and your friend
 s and family. Refreshments will be provided. Ingredient list will be ava
 ilable at the program.\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 1st Floor\, Children's Programming Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa062565ecd9e1b553241c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
