BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Friday Film Club: Bride of Frankenstein
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T150000
UID:6ab42ef8129d8e0031f49398@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of the Universal Pictures horror clas
 sic\nBride of Frankenstein\n(1935\, director James Whale).\nBoris Karloff 
 reprises his role as the silver screen's most misunderstood monster\, who 
 now longs for a mate (played by the haunting Elsa Lanchester).\nFilm Runti
 me: 1 Hour & 15 Minutes.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, 3rd Floor\, Room B
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab42ef8129d8e0031f49398
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How To Volunteer To Build Skills And Gain Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T193000
UID:6a3938a1ba0ec7dc2261cd76@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in this free information session and discover how to s
 afely get involved as a volunteer to gain skills and build your resume. In
  this session you will:\nLearn how to start your formal volunteering.\nUnd
 erstand how to use Volunteer Toronto's website to search for opportunities
  that best match your interests and skills.\nSet expectations for what to 
 expect after you apply for a volunteer role.\nDiscuss how to use volunteer
 ing to build your resume and gain skills.\nThis session is great for anyon
 e who wants to make a positive impact on our city or learn new skills.\nPr
 esented by\nVolunteer Toronto\n.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room\, Basement Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3938a1ba0ec7dc2261cd76
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Garden with Purpose: Practical Ecological Gardening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T150000
UID:6aab19538cf597003f9462a5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover the core principles of ecological gardening and learn
  how to transform your garden into a space that’s both environmentally r
 esponsible and visually stunning. A Toronto Master Gardener will provide g
 uidance on how to create habitat\, manage water wisely\, and reduce your e
 cological impact — all while cultivating a landscape rich with beauty an
 d year-round interest. Suitable for gardeners of any skill level\, with an
 y kind of outdoor space.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Plane
 t\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South
  Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aab19538cf597003f9462a5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
