BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Career Confidence & Wellness Series: Career Stress & Anxiety
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T180000
UID:6abad13429c3d600332c3d01@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Feeling stressed or anxious about your career? We’ll explore
  how anxiety manifests in the mind and body\, and learn to recognize your 
 own patterns of anxiety\, challenge unhelpful thinking habits\, and practi
 ce strategies for staying grounded when career stress feels overwhelming. 
 Through reflection\, discussion\, and a real-life case study\, you’ll ga
 in skills to respond differently to career uncertainty\, while developing 
 a more compassionate and flexible mindset.\nThis program is part of TPL's 
 Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor 
 Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends 
 of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nThe William and Nona Heasli
 p Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach\nNe
 ed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoo
 m Privacy Statement\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abad13429c3d600332c3d01
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board Games for Adults: Wednesday Afternoon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T160000
UID:69a204c61e64afd01e5e9198@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the fun of playing modern and classic board games!
 \nDrop in with your friends (or make some new ones) and play games like:\n
 Anomia\, Backgammon\, Bananagrams\, Chess\, CodeNames\, Connect Four\, Ex
 ploding Kittens\, Monopoly\, Quirkle\, Rumikub\, Scrabble\, Set\, Settlers
  of Catan\, Snakes and Ladders\, Sorry\, SushiGO\, UNO\, UpWords and ma
 ny more!\nPlease don't hesitate to call us or visit the red desk on the fi
 rst floor if you have any questions.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a204c61e64afd01e5e9198
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
