BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Magic and Illusion Workshop for Young Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T193000
UID:6a8ccbe569166f088b9498a6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Take a journey into the mysteries of magical illusions. Local 
 magician Ayan Deb explores the science and art of deception and illusion. 
 In this interactive workshop\, participants will enjoy and watch a series 
 of the newest tricks in the world of magic. Participants will also get a c
 hance to learn some simple\, yet astonishing magic tricks using everyday o
 bjects. Drop in.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8ccbe569166f088b9498a6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The A(i) B\, C's of Artificial Intelligence - the AI literacy show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T193000
UID:6a6e55f83f18b57d5232973f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The”A(i)\, B\, C’s of AI literacy – the AI literacy show
 ” is a 90 minute\, dynamic performance/presentation hosted by Keith McDo
 nald\, founder and Chief Curator of Toronto’s “the literacyAI project
 ”. Keith covers four must know AI areas in a fun\, easy to understand wa
 y and also presents a compelling case for making Artificial Intelligence l
 iteracy a must have in schools and in business.\nNote: This is an interact
 ive\, multi-media presentation with audience interaction\, video clips\, p
 rops\, and includes an opening AI literacy song ice breaker. Attendees do 
 not have to know coding as this is very much a non-technical presentation 
 with time for Q/A with the audience.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6e55f83f18b57d5232973f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
