BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Housing Day: A Film Screening and Panel Discussion of See
 king Shelter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T200000
UID:6abe6ad011bbf300684aa557@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:On November 24\nth\n\, join Homeless Connect Toronto at the To
 ronto Reference Library for a special premiere screening and community con
 versation celebrating the launch of Seeking Shelter\, a documentary series
  by filmmaker Nadine Valcin.\nAs Canada continues to grapple with a growin
 g housing crisis\, Seeking Shelter shines a light on the people\, organiza
 tions\, and grassroots movements creating innovative and inclusive solutio
 ns to housing instability. Through stories of resilience\, collaboration\,
  and community action\, the series explores what becomes possible when peo
 ple come together to reimagine housing.\nThis special event will feature p
 remiere screenings of:\nEpisode 2: Communal Land for the Common Good :\nTo
 ronto’s Parkdale Neighbourhood Land Trust is sowing the seeds for innova
 tive housing and communal growth.\nAnd\nEpisode 3: Co-ops and the Power of
  Community:\nSince the 1970s\, a Toronto co-operative has modelled a colla
 borative and people-first approach to housing.\nFollowing the screenings\,
  filmmaker Nadine Valcin will moderate a panel discussion with housing sub
 ject-matter experts\, exploring the themes raised in the films and the fut
 ure of community-driven housing solutions. Audience members will also have
  an opportunity to participate in a Q&A and contribute reflections to a co
 llaborative poll.\nDoors open: 6pm\nThe episodes are provided courtesy of 
 the National Film Board of Canada.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall (1st floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe6ad011bbf300684aa557
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
