BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Tanveer Khan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T235959
UID:6abe717f9abb62002c6b6e89@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of\nOctober\, Postcards of the Everyday b
 y\nTanveer Khan\nare on display at\nMorningside branch\nTanveer Khan is a 
 Toronto-based photographer whose work captures the quiet beauty of everyda
 y life in cities and along coastlines. She explores how neighbourhoods\, s
 treets\, and architecture hold memory and belonging. Trained as an enginee
 r\, Tanveer brings a balance of precision and curiosity to her creative pr
 actice. Using 35mm film\, she focuses on ordinary yet timeless scenes\, cr
 eating images that invite reflection\, nostalgia and a sense of connection
  across places and moments.\n"\nI work with 35mm film to preserve the flee
 ting\, ordinary moments that shape our sense of home — a streetcar slipp
 ing by\, laundry strung above an alley\, or the soft glow of a harbour at 
 dusk. Having lived in India\, the Middle East\, and now Canada\, I’ve co
 me to see how neighbourhoods across the world share subtle echoes of one a
 nother. Through my camera\, I collect these echoes like postcards from dif
 ferent cities — quiet stories stitched together through light\, shadow\,
  and memory."\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibit program\n. Toron
 to Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work a
 t locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cul
 tural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nFree. All are welcome
 .\nTitle of Piece: The Fence King Medium (e.g. oil\, acrylic\, photography
 \, etc.): Photography\, Digital Inkjet Print Size/Dimensions: Medium
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe717f9abb62002c6b6e89
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
