SUMMARY:Public Speaking for Newcomers: Communicate with Confidence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T140000
UID:6a92f312aafa610029600470@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Communicating clearly and confidently is a skill that everyone
  should have. For newcomers\, public speaking can feel especially daunting
  when navigating a new language or cultural expectations. This session is 
 designed to help you overcome those challenges and approach public speakin
 g with confidence. Along many educational and professional paths in Canada
 \, giving presentations is often a requirement. This session will provide 
 an overview of how to design and deliver presentations\, while also offeri
 ng practical tips and techniques for speaking clearly and effectively in a
  new environment.\nThis program is part of Small Business Month and the Ne
 wcomer Entrepreneurship Initiative.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe P
 ersonal Information on this form is collection by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.​
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a92f312aafa610029600470
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
