BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "From Insulin to Islet Transplants: Canada's ongoing 
 contribution to diabetes research" with Krista Lamb
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T190000
UID:6a8f1249b20478002995ad01@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Since Banting’s discovery of insulin at U of T in 1921\, Can
 adian scientists have remained on the front lines of the development of ne
 w treatments for diabetes\, and the quest for a cure. Around the globe\, p
 eople with diabetes are benefiting from breakthroughs with a Canadian conn
 ection.\nAuthor Krista Lamb (\nBeyond Banting\n) shares stories about the 
 remarkable scientists from across the country who are building on Banting
 ’s legacy.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Davenport\, Second Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f1249b20478002995ad01
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Personal Library App
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6a9b51b41c197d11325d7023@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build your own personal library app\, just b
 y describing it?\nIn this class\, you'll use an AI coding assistant to bui
 ld a small app for your reading life: add books you've read and books you 
 want to read\, keep your whole list in one private place\, and link each b
 ook to the library catalogue so placing a hold is one click away. You'll l
 earn the build loop: describe what you want\, review the plan\, build one 
 feature\, test it\, fix the bugs. Your reading list stays on your own comp
 uter. The library keeps the books\; this file keeps your reading life\, an
 d it travels with you.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet s
 kills. Computers are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistrat
 ion is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your s
 pot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nA
 fter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on a first come\, first se
 rve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from t
 his hands-on program\, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tool
 s Used in This Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic 
 AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create you
 r own account for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the
  Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices 
 on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each to
 ol prior to attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the too
 l\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview
  privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview pr
 ivacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy 
 policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
 d for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions 
 about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerli
 ne staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toron
 to ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b41c197d11325d7023
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
