SUMMARY:Buying a Car? Know Your Rights!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T160000
UID:6a8db51860ccaf01c020dea3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month.\nBuying a vehicle can be
  a challenging experience with long-term financial implications.\nJoin us 
 for an online presentation by the\nOntario Motor Vehicle Industry Council 
 (OMVIC)\n\, the regulator of motor vehicle sales in Ontario. A representat
 ive from OMVIC will provide you with resources and tips for buying new and
  used cars in Ontario.\nTopics will include:\nOMVIC’s Compensation Fund\
 nUnderstanding Car Dealer Advertising\nNegative Equity & Long Term Loans\n
 Agreement & Disclosure\nAvoiding Curbsides & Fraud Prevention\nTips for Bu
 ying or Leasing a Car\nRegistration:\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to j
 oin. Once registered\, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link.\nNeed
  help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom 
 Privacy Statement\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informatio
 n on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public
  Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will 
 only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed 
 to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Str
 eet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8db51860ccaf01c020dea3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
