DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T200000
UID:6a9b4e2d1c197d11325d6f1d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Job hunting is a job in itself: applications\, deadlines\, int
 erviews\, follow-ups. What if you could build your own AI-powered system t
 o help you manage it?\nIn this hands-on class with our Innovator-in-Reside
 nce\,\nRyan Kelln\n\, you'll explore a job-hunting dashboard built with AI
 : how it tracks applications\, sets automatic alerts for postings that mat
 ch you\, and practices interviews with you through role-play. You'll leave
  with the templates to build your own. We'll also talk about how employers
  screen applications\, and how it can make things unfair. Come explore a t
 ool that works for you\, not the other way around.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\
 , keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding exp
 erience required. If you wish to save your work from this hands-on progra
 m\, please bring your own USB stick.\nRegistration is required and will st
 art September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed
