BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Career Confidence & Wellness Series: Rebounding from Rejection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T180000
UID:6ab6cb6686d845003118c20c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Has a job rejection\, unanswered application\, or difficult in
 terview affected your confidence? We’ll explore the emotional and cognit
 ive impact of career setbacks and how to respond without letting rejection
  disarm your confidence or your next steps. You’ll learn how to identify
  what is within your control\, and reframe rejection as an opportunity to 
 learn and explore new possibilities. Through interactive activities and re
 flection\, you’ll develop strategies for self-care\, confidence\, and re
 silience.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and i
 s generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with sup
 porting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South
  Chapter and\nWilliam and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\,
  please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6cb6686d845003118c20c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Delicious and Surprising History of The Dining Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T150000
UID:6a31bed6caf9343600639830@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:John Ota presents​ and discusses his book\,\nThe Dining Room
  : Exploring the Design of Twelve Iconic Rooms in Search of the Perfect Di
 ning Experience.​\n​(Random House\, 2026).\nExplore the stories behind
  twelve iconic dining rooms in homes around the world—from a Japanese sa
 murai house to Claude Monet's brilliant yellow dining room to Frida Kahlo'
 s Casa Azul to Jackie Kennedy’s White House—and travel through time in
  pursuit of the ultimate design.​\nThe Dining Room is an englightening a
 nd joyous celebration of history\, culture and the art of dning. Presenter
  John Ota's charming observations of the surprising impact of dining rooms
  on our lives and the cherised moments we share within them will delight a
 rmchair travellers\, history fanatics and interior design enthusiasts alik
 e.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a31bed6caf9343600639830
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
