DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T160000
UID:6abe8d069d27a000454de05b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in learning more about your rights?\nJoin u
 s for an interactive and informative session with the\nCanadian Civil Libe
 rties Education Trust (CCLET).\nWe will discuss the Charter of Rights and 
 Freedoms\, the Ontario Human Rights Code\, and rights and freedoms in Cana
 da – including freedom of expression\, protest rights\, protections agai
 nst discrimination and more!\nLogo for CCLET - Canadian Civil Liberties Ed
 ucation Trust\nToronto's municipal election takes place on October 26\, 20
 26. Check out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\
 npage to learn more about the upcoming election\, access important voter r
 esources\, and discover more activities and interactive library programs f
 or all ages happening at a branch near you.\nThis initiative is made possi
 ble by donations to the Toronto Public Library Foundation and is generousl
 y supported by the McConnell Foundation
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 101\, first floor
