DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T153000
UID:6a2850561e67cd9cb338adb9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How do we tell powerful stories that matter? Stories that expl
 ore family secrets\, confront historical injustices or give voice to margi
 nalized experiences while upholding ethical responsibilities and honoring 
 the complexities of truth?\nAuthor Caroline Topperman\n(Your Roots Cast a 
 Shadow)\nwill lead this writers' workshop that delves into the intricate p
 rocess of writing creative nonfiction that tackles challenging subjects\, 
 particularly those related to family\, displacement\, estrangement\, and i
 mmigration.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
