DESCRIPTION:November is Financial Literacy Month!\nTake charge of your fin
 ancial future with practical tools and strategies to help you budget wisel
 y\, make informed financial decisions\, and protect yourself from common s
 cams. Join financial literacy staff from North York Community House for an
  informative session on budgeting and money management. Learn practical st
 rategies for creating a budget\, understanding the pros and cons of credit
  cards\, accessing government benefits through tax filing\, and protecting
  yourself from frauds and scams.\nFollowing the presentation\, there will 
 be an opportunity to ask questions and connect with Financial Empowerment 
 staff for additional support.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac95e84f34d34366b3c6952
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Real Ghosts: A Hallowe'en Exclusive
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261031T160000
UID:6aa43593d6577100383c9942@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Putting the ‘boo’ in ‘book’\, author Peter Roe (\nHaun
 ted Town Halls\n\,\nThe Complete Paranormal  Investigation Handbook\n) wil
 l manifest at the Mimico Centennial Library\, for an exclusive Hallowe’e
 n visit Saturday\, October 31st\, at 2:30 pm sharing\nThe Searcher Group
 ’\ns true-life discoveries from the field of ghost investigation.\nOver 
 30 years before reality TV inspired thousands of thrill-seeking groups wor
 ldwide\,\nThe Searcher Group\n– Canada’s oldest\, most reputable and a
 ccomplished paranormal research team – celebrates its 47\nth\nAnniversar
 y in 2026!\nMixing chills\, a deep appreciation of Ontario’s vanishing h
 eritage and thought-provoking discussion with a dash of humour\, this popu
 lar presentation returns discussing tools-of-the-trade\, original theory o
 n life-after-life phenomena and rarely-seen ghost photos!\nSkeptics and th
 e curious alike are all welcome to attend this judgment-free Hallowe’en 
 event. Bring your own inquiries and experiences to a Q&A following the hou
 r-long talk!\nFor early attendees eager to secure a seat\, a Pre-Show vide
 o will start at 2:00 pm\, to set the mood.\nCopies of\nHaunted Town Halls\
 n($20) and/or\nThe Complete Paranormal Investigation Handbook\n($30) will 
 be available for sale and signing with no obligation to purchase. Cash onl
 y\, please.\n*Please Note: Video recordings of this presentation are not p
 ermitted\, thank you.\nAbout the Presenter\nAs Assistant Director of The S
 earcher Group (TSG)\, Peter Roe also serves as Director of TSG subdivision
 \, Mortal Coil Paranormal (MCP)\, serving the Greater Toronto Area and sou
 thwestern Ontario.\nWhen he is not spearheading investigations and conduct
 ing research\, he is actively promoting TSG’s pro bono services\, public
 ly presenting field discoveries and advocating against Ontario’s rapidly
  vanishing heritage.\nPeter has appeared in a testimonial capacity over tw
 o seasons of the Travel Channel’s Fear the Woods (aka Evil Encounters on
  T+E Channel)\, been interviewed by CBC Radio and the Paranormal UK Networ
 k\, and has earned worldwide notoriety with the release of his first nonfi
 ction publication\, Haunted Town Halls (Quagmire Press)\, in 2018.\nPeter 
 is co-author of\nThe Complete Paranormal Investigation Handbook\nwith Sear
 cher Group founder Richard Palmisano – released August 18\, 2025 through
  Llewellyn Worldwide.\nAbout The Searcher Group\nFounded in 1979 by Richar
 d Palmisano\, The Searcher Group (TSG) is Canada’s leading team of inves
 tigators\, researchers and theorists. The Searcher Group’s mission inclu
 des investigating alleged paranormal activity\, developing and conducting 
 experiments for the advancement of parapsychology\, and researching and de
 veloping new technologies and theoretic models.\nBoasting an ironclad repu
 tation for safety\, confidentiality and credibility over the course of 47 
 years\, TSG has had the privilege of working with government officials and
  operators of recognized\, historic public sites alike\, in its ongoing qu
 est to discover and contribute answers to humankind’s most enduring ques
 tions pertaining to life-after-life and ghost phenomena.\nApplying his 37-
 year career in law enforcement\, security and surveillance in the field\, 
 Richard is also the author of five nonfiction publications documenting the
  team’s most harrowing and informative cases\, including\nOvershadows\n(
 2003)\,\nJourneys into the Unknown\n(2006)\,\nGhosts\n(2009)\,\nGhosts of 
 the Canadian National Exhibition\n(2011) and\nMeeting Place of the Dead\n(
 2014)\, all available through Dundurn Press. He has co-authored an advance
 d paranormal investigation manual with TSG Assistant Director Peter Roe\, 
 titled The Complete Paranormal Investigation Handbook released August 18\,
  2025 through Llewellyn Worldwide.\nRichard and his books have been featur
 ed on television\, radio and internet podcasts worldwide\, including A Hau
 nting (Season 1\, Discovery Channel)\, Northern Mysteries\, Portal into th
 e Unknown\, CBC Radio\, Breakfast Television\, Darkness Radio\, and Crash 
 Course in Awesome\, among many others.\nThe Searcher Group featured as the
  cover story of the United Church Observer (now\nBroadview\n) in October 2
 016* and soon after appeared in Reader’s Digest (April 2017)
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa43593d6577100383c9942
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
