UID:6abe6870754bb0003ac29165@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This interactive workshop will help you uncover the transferab
 le skills you have already developed through work\, volunteer roles\, educ
 ation\, and life experiences. Participants will learn how to identify the 
 capabilities employers value most\, analyze job descriptions to determine 
 which skills matter for a target role\, and map their experience to those 
 requirements. By the end of the session\, you will have a clearer understa
 nding of your strengths and a practical framework for recognizing the valu
 e you already bring to a career transition.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoin
 ing and participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nThis p
 rogram is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supp
 orted by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fi
 delity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nThe
  William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit
 \ntpl.ca/careercoach
