DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T190000
UID:6ab2b31a607483003828c1ed@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. This 
 session is a condensed overview of building a WordPress website from start
  to finish - covering the basics of domain and hosting\, the WordPress das
 hboard\, plugins\, design and branding\, and adding an online shop with Wo
 oCommerce. This program is catered to newcomer entrepreneurs but is open
  to anyone looking to build a website.\nBy the end\, participants will hav
 e a clear understanding of what's involved\, how long it takes\, and wheth
 er building their own website is the right fit for them. No experience nee
 ded.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2b31a607483003828c1ed
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
