SUMMARY:Geometric Arts and Watercolour Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T160000
UID:6aa979093dd190003e721c1e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an ex
 tensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heavil
 y on tools such as protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this workshop\
 , participants will be guided by artist Farooq Zia through step-by-step in
 structions using drawing tools and watercolour paint to create their own g
 eometric pattern and complex design art pieces.\nDrop-in\, no registration
  required.\nAll adults welcome.\nSpace is limited.\nProgram will be capped
  at the first 15 participants.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa979093dd190003e721c1e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
