BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The 5 Pieces of the AI Puzzle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:6a6bbc1224cc9f017dda0999@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Artificial Intelligence researchers agree: citizens are having
  varied reactions to the complexity and transitional nature of AI. If you
  agree - and believe the need for understanding our current and coming hum
 an relationships with AI is at a premium -  you will want to attend this 
 presentation.\nKeith McDonald\, from Toronto's the literacy AI project\, p
 resents a 60 minute session using a 5 piece puzzle as an illuminating met
 aphor. Each of the 5 pieces represents a separate but critical aspect towa
 rd laying the foundation for understanding Artificial Intelligence in an 
 entertaining\, clear and easy to digest way.\nRegistration is limited to 1
 5 people
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6bbc1224cc9f017dda0999
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
