BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newsgirls: Gutsy Pioneers in Canada’s Newsrooms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261023T113000
UID:6abe922b035faf0033d99381@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto author\, freelance writer and former Toronto Star repo
 rter\, Donna Jean Mackinnon\, presents her book\nNewgirls: Gutsy Pioneers 
 in Canada’s Newsrooms\n(Leaping Lion Books\, 2017).\nIn Newsgirls\, Mack
 innon documents the lives of 10 leading female reporters who started their
  careers during newspaper's Golden Age. This fascinating\, often amusing\,
  presentation will include a slew of vintage photos and intimate anecdotes
 . Trailblazers in their fields\, these adventurous 'newshens'\, as they we
 re once called\, covered every beat from art openings\, fashion\, crime\, 
 politics to major social issues of the day​.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe922b035faf0033d99381
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
