DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T143000
UID:6ac513789abb62002c6c9a0f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This session will help participants understand how the job mar
 ket is evolving and how to stay competitive in a changing workforce. Parti
 cipants will explore current trends in recruiting and hiring\, learn why c
 ontinuous learning and skill development are essential for long-term caree
 r success\, and gain insight into the growing gig economy and its impact o
 n work opportunities in Canada. The session will also highlight emerging t
 echnologies that are shaping the job search process and help participants 
 prepare for the future of work.\nThis workshop is presented by ACCES Empl
 oyment Toronto\, focused on supporting jobseekers and employers with a va
 riety of specialized programs and resources both in-person and online.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
