SUMMARY:Who Should Own AI? Building Public AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261121T160000
UID:6a9b51abaafa61002961b2a3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:If AI becomes as important as roads\, electricity\, or librari
 es\, who should own it? Who decides what it's used for? Who gets access an
 d to say no?\nThis panel discussion\, as part of our Innovator-in-Residen
 ce program with\nRyan Kelln\n\, will include speakers building public-int
 erest AI\, working in civic tech\, and organizing communities affected by 
 AI decisions. We'll explore what's already being built\, from open models 
 and public compute to community-owned data\, and what's being privatized. 
 You'll get to draft your own "public AI requirements" and see what others 
 think should be guaranteed to everyone. The future of AI is being decided 
 now\; this is a chance to have a say in it.\nFeaturing:\nAlex Olson\n\, Di
 rector of University of Toronto’s Centre for Analytics & AI Engineering\
 nKhasir Hean\n\, Founder of Technologists for Democracy\, Machine Learning
  engineer\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:
 30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the star
 t of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on a f
 irst come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@
 tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51abaafa61002961b2a3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
