BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python V
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T200000
UID:6a97332669166f088b9690d2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this follow up course we will take a break from the logical side of 
 back-end development and get our feet wet with a little bit of front-end c
 oding\; we'll make a user interface! Using tkinter\, a popular module for 
 creating user-facing layouts\, we will design and implement a simple but e
 ffective UI for our Python code. This will allow us to run our programs us
 ing another platform other than Terminal.\nThis class is for beginners but
  assumes you have a basic understanding of Python or have attended Coding 
 with Python I\, II\, III\, and IV.\nRegistration will start 2 weeks before
  this class\n. This program is hosted on Zoom. The Zoom information and l
 ink will be shared over email.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe person
 al information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library und
 er the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The info
 rmation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery an
 d evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can
  be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a97332669166f088b9690d2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
