BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trust\, Participation and Democracy: What Canadians Are Saying
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T193000
UID:6a99ae1baafa610029615271@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Trust in democratic institutions is being challenged in Canada
  and around the world. While many Canadians still believe in democratic va
 lues\, more people are worried about political divisions\, lower trust in 
 governments and public institutions\, false information\, and whether poli
 tical systems are meeting people's needs.\nUsing the latest public opinion
  polls\, election research\, and public engagement data\, this panel will 
 explore how Canadians feel about democracy today. Are concerns about democ
 racy shared by many Canadians\, or are they more common in certain groups?
  What is causing changes in political trust and participation? And what ca
 n governments\, community organizations\, educators\, and local communitie
 s do to help strengthen democracy and encourage people to get involved in 
 the future?\nFeaturing\nAndrew Parkin\n\, Executive Director\,\nEnvironics
  Institute\nSarah Morra\,\nChair\, Vote 16 Canada and Research Assistant\,
 \nThe Samara Centre for Democracy\nJoanna Massie\,\nPostdoctoral Fellow in
  Political Science\,\nMcMaster University\nModerator:\nShawn Micallef\n\, 
 Toronto Star columnist & University of Toronto civics instructor\nToronto'
 s municipal election takes place on October 26\, 2026. Check out the\nKnow
 YourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\npage to learn more abou
 t the upcoming election\, access important voter resources\, and discover 
 activities and interactive library programs for all ages happening at a br
 anch near you.\nThis initiative is made possible by donations to the Toron
 to Public Library Foundation and is generously supported by the McConnell 
 Foundation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ae1baafa610029615271
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
