SUMMARY:Lead Where You Are: Building Leadership Skills for the Workplace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T180000
UID:6ab6ccfe60748300382988e5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Leadership does not begin with a management title. This practi
 cal workshop helps young professionals understand different leadership app
 roaches and develop the skills to lead effectively at their current stage 
 of life and career. Through relatable workplace situations\, participants 
 will explore communication\, collaboration\, initiative\, accountability a
 nd decision-making\, and learn how to put these skills into practice in th
 eir everyday professional lives.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and par
 ticipating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nThis program is p
 art of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by ou
 r lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Cana
 da\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nThe William an
 d Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/ca
 reercoach
