BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for Us: Shaping AI in Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261205T160000
UID:6a9b51beaafa61002961b2a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto is one of the biggest AI cities in the world. But what
  do the people here actually think about it and how do we want to shape it
 s development and use?\nA panel of experts\, alongside our Innovator-in-Re
 sidence\nRyan Kelln\n\, who know AI from very different angles\, unite fo
 r an open conversation about what AI is doing to this city\, and what we w
 ant it to do instead. We'll talk about:\nThe human beings behind the machi
 nes: what drives the people who build AI\, and what worries them.\nWork\, 
 money\, and meaning: what happens to jobs\, creativity\, and value when AI
  lands here.\nWho gets to shape it and who's left out (both are our neighb
 ours).\nThe stories we tell: how art\, media\, news\, and everyday talk sh
 ape what we expect\, fear\, and hope for.\nNo pitches\, no boosterism. Jus
 t an honest conversation about the ideas and stories shaping AI in this ci
 ty\, and what we want it to become.\nFeaturing:\nJerrold McGrath\n\, Cultu
 ral Programmer and Theorist\, In the Meantime\nJoseph Wilson\n\, Anthropol
 ogist & Author of Humans of AI: Understanding the Humans Behind the Machin
 es\nOwais Lightwala\n\, Assistant Professor\, Performance at The Creative 
 School at Toronto Metropolitan University\, Director\,\nChrysalis\nRegistr
 ation is required and will start November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: You
 r spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.
 \nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be filled on a first come\, first
  serve basis until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51beaafa61002961b2a7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
